{
  "dom_id": "step-q44321",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "The trinomial $4{x}^{2}{z}^{6}+8x{z}^{6}-60{z}^{6}$ is equivalent to",
  "worked_solution": "Note that all of the terms have a common factor of $4{z}^{6}.$ To simplify the computation, we can factor out the $4{z}^{6},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}{z}^{6}+8x{z}^{6}-60{z}^{6}=(4{z}^{6})\\cdot {x}^{2}+(4{z}^{6})\\cdot 2x-(4{z}^{6})\\cdot 15=4{z}^{6}({x}^{2}+2x-15).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the polynomial ${x}^{2}+2x-15,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{z}^{6}({x}^{2}+2x-15) & = \\\\ 4{z}^{6}(({x}^{2}+5x)+(-3x-15)) & = \\\\ 4{z}^{6}(x(x+5)-3(x+5)) & = \\\\ 4{z}^{6}(x-3)(x+5)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
